{"title":"1988 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 1988 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider 2 concentric circle radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51f9145defed0bd27aee6cb2952813f8ae4a758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R &gt; r$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />) with centre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c79ddff6b45c6ad853d03d6231fdf0fba5ededb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> Fix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on the small circle and consider the variable chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> of the small circle. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the large circle; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79fff1317b48a57146bc1936964b9e381ee87824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B,P,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bb7c232e71ec1b8993ad4a38488d71e3490cf4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP.$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>i.) For which values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c94322485112d08cc14f837f01681b978862e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OPA$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> is the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade8f10cacf4f6d91a582328fa0c21f96e0330ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^2 + CA^2 + AB^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" /> extremal?\n</p><p>ii.) What are the possible positions of the midpoints <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c94322485112d08cc14f837f01681b978862e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OPA$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> varies?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be an even positive integer. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa7de55a64e20580a4f7db3b3fd446248c5de60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_{n + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" /> be sets having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> elements each such that any two of them have exactly one element in common while every element of their union belongs to at least two of the given sets. For which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can one assign to every element of the union one of the numbers 0 and 1 in such a manner that each of the sets has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f752db018007f35ab62c4bcd31a5f380cd4d1282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" /> zeros?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> defined on the positive integers (and taking positive integers values) is given by:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66ca3b700af279d616ab9c8818efa6361cbe2cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix} f(1) = 1, f(3) = 3 \\\\ f(2 \\cdot n) = f(n) \\\\ f(4 \\cdot n + 1) = 2 \\cdot f(2 \\cdot n + 1) - f(n) \\\\ f(4 \\cdot n + 3) = 3 \\cdot f(2 \\cdot n + 1) - 2 \\cdot f(n), \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -34px\" width=\"309\" height=\"78\" />\n</p><p>for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> Determine with proof the number of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/813b58104d0c43e6351e7b6127b2758d01c902ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq 1988$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/5/cd5d064761fa0ec9b4febecdc5a988047f837e6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Show that the solution set of the inequality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac7df0a9a7a36456ad31615aced9a17c3d870953.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum^{70}_{k = 1} \\frac {k}{x - k} \\geq \\frac {5}{4}\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"51\" />\nis a union of disjoint intervals, the sum of whose length is 1988.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a right-angled triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be the altitude drawn to the hypotenuse and let the straight line joining the incentres of the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/2333c7e3153eedc0e2f856f84de41ff67e617df1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD, ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> intersect the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547f225d9af24dda08195ad51ee009872c3d3fc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> at the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/9141cf60419b778a5a3a2d5c6ef4d5e5200ff45a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K,L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459b08d5235f417c69f0cc0c2d473a4739abdb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> denote the areas of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7439149f594e9b8f42ef995654a5cf9d644b5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AKL$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> respectively, show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/67878b24ad731c2b6823a11a88ba4f7a9348aa49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {E}{E_1} \\geq 2.\\]\" width=\"59\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be two positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/2579953d20a3ecb93cfde993fe8f138702e4bcf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\cdot b + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73dbae0d4cab732558228057baa3c3c8b389db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2} + b^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/825af8e1206386b7aa6ceeffc11703bf0ad4b2e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {a^{2} + b^{2}}{a \\cdot b + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"64\" height=\"40\" /> is a perfect square.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO\" title=\"1988 IMO\">1988 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1988\">IMO 1988 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO\" title=\"1988 IMO\">1988 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO\" title=\"1987 IMO\">1987 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO\" title=\"1989 IMO\">1989 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043313\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 261/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 837/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7712/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.616      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.616      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18226:|#|:idhash:canonical and 